## Principles

- Markdown is the source of truth; committee and board versions are circulated as Word (.docx).
- Board papers authorise direction (VESEP application and funding model), not final dollar figures.
- Scope is organised by area, not by priority tier; the project is a single coordinated program.
- Do not reinstate items Nick has deliberately removed without asking.
- For mechanical design: run the fabricator-review pass before producing drawings, never after. Validate stack-ups at the design phase; resolve all issues in the spec sheet first, then draw.
- Ask up front about interfaced equipment, receiving fixtures, site constraints, and structural sign-off requirements before any fabrication design proceeds.

## Constraints

- **VESEP funding model is fixed at 2:1** (government:club). Club share = one-third of total project cost.
- **Club contribution mechanism:** term deposit drawn at maturity; repaid from 50% of net functions revenue. Estimated repayment under six months at current performance.
- **Term deposit balance and maturity date are not yet confirmed** -- final figures paper cannot be prepared until these are known.
- **All item costs are $TBC** -- no quotes have been obtained; the master plan carries placeholders.
- **Stable area IDs** are the reference system across all documents: OFF-##, HAL-##, FB-##, CHG-##, GS-##, KIT-##, CLN-##, PA-##, SEC-##, BLD-##, EXT-##, PT-##.
- **Board-rack Rev-A** partly supersedes the original five SVGs; Rev-B final pack is in design.
- **Output format:** Markdown source of truth; .docx for board and committee circulation.
- Australian English, no em dashes, executive tone throughout all documents.

## Goal

The board endorses the Clubhouse Renewal Proposal, authorising a VESEP application and the term-deposit funding model. The sponsor then obtains firm quotes for all items, engages LSV on VESEP round dates and eligibility, and returns to the board with final figures before any binding commitment.

In parallel, the GS-03 board-rack drawing pack reaches Rev-B fabricator-ready status: stack-ups verified at the design phase, fabricator pre-flight completed before drawings are produced, and a dimensioned drawing pack a fabricator can build from directly.

Done is measured by: board resolution on file, all quotes obtained, VESEP application package prepared, and Rev-B drawing pack complete and fabricator-reviewed.

